  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "When a gas filled in a closed vessel is heated by raising the temperature by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, its pressure increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math> The initial temperature of the gas is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "250",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From ideal gas equation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is amount of substance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is ideal gas constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;is volume.</p><p>In closed vessel volume remains constant.</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>",
